{"y":2009,"label":"2008–09","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":31,"l":5,"cw":15,"cl":3,"confFinish":"3rd in Big East","finish":"final4","seed":1,"region":"West","apPre":2,"apHigh":1,"apFinal":5,"srs":22.17,"sos":8.57,"ortg":112.2,"drtg":92.1,"ppg":78.3,"oppg":64.2,"story":{"headline":"Six Overtimes and a Final Four","text":"Preseason No. 2 with its starting five back plus McDonald's All-American Kemba Walker, UConn won the Paradise Jam, beat No. 8 Gonzaga 88–83 in overtime in Seattle and rose to No. 1 in February. Jim Calhoun won his 800th game at Marquette on February 25, but the Huskies lost Jerome Dyson to a knee injury against Syracuse. Hasheem Thabeet shared Big East Player of the Year with Pitt's DeJuan Blair and was national defensive player of the year. In the Big East quarterfinals, UConn and Syracuse played an epic six-overtime game at Madison Square Garden that ended at 1:22 a.m. — Syracuse winning 127–117. The Huskies still earned a No. 1 seed, beat Chattanooga, Texas A&M and Purdue, then Missouri 82–75 behind 23 points from Walker for their third Final Four. Michigan State ended the run 82–73 in Detroit. Thabeet went No. 2 in the draft.","moments":[{"date":"2009-02-25","title":"Calhoun's 800th win","text":"Jim Calhoun earns career win No. 800 at Marquette's Bradley Center."},{"date":"2009-03-12","title":"Six overtimes","text":"Syracuse beats UConn 127–117 in six overtimes in the Big East quarterfinals, ending at 1:22 a.m."},{"date":"2009-03-19","title":"NCAA First Round: W vs Chattanooga","text":"UConn beat Chattanooga 103–47 in the NCAA tournament first round at Wachovia Center, Philadelphia, PA."},{"date":"2009-03-21","title":"NCAA Second Round: W vs Texas A&M","text":"UConn beat Texas A&M 92–66 in the NCAA tournament second round at Wachovia Center, Philadelphia, PA."},{"date":"2009-03-26","title":"NCAA Sweet Sixteen: W vs Purdue","text":"UConn beat Purdue 72–60 in the NCAA tournament sweet sixteen at University of Phoenix Stadium, Glendale, AZ."},{"date":"2009-03-28","title":"NCAA Elite Eight: W vs Missouri","text":"UConn beat Missouri 82–75 in the NCAA tournament elite eight at University of Phoenix Stadium, Glendale, AZ."},{"date":"2009-04-04","title":"NCAA Final Four: L vs Michigan State","text":"UConn lost to Michigan State 73–82 in the NCAA tournament final four at Ford Field, Detroit, MI."}],"honors":["Paradise Jam tournament champions","NCAA Final Four","Hasheem Thabeet – Consensus second-team All-American","Hasheem Thabeet – NABC Defensive Player of the Year","Hasheem Thabeet – Big East Co-Player of the Year","Hasheem Thabeet – Big East Defensive Player of the Year","A.J. Price – NCAA Regional Most Outstanding Player","Hasheem Thabeet – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008%E2%80%9309_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Calhoun","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasheem_Thabeet","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kemba_Walker","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Price","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syracuse%E2%80%93UConn_rivalry"]},"roster":[{"pid":"aj-price-1","name":"A.J. Price","num":"12","cls":"SR","pos":"G","ht":"6-2","wt":181,"home":"Amityville, NY","rsci":"24 ( 2004 )","photo":"assets/players/aj-price-1.jpg","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":35,"gs":35,"mp":31.8,"pts":14.7,"trb":3.5,"ast":4.7,"stl":0.7,"blk":0.0,"tov":2.7,"fg_pct":0.408,"fg3_pct":0.402,"ft_pct":0.721,"orb":0.6,"pf":1.3},"tot":{"mp":1112,"fg":170,"fga":417,"fg3":82,"fg3a":204,"ft":93,"fta":129,"orb":20,"drb":102,"trb":122,"ast":164,"stl":24,"blk":0,"tov":94,"pf":44,"pts":515,"g":35},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.538,"efg_pct":0.506,"usg_pct":25.1,"ast_pct":28.2,"trb_pct":5.8,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":0.0,"ws":4.0,"ws_per_40":0.144,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null}},{"pid":"jeff-adrien-1","name":"Jeff Adrien","num":"4","cls":"SR","pos":"F","ht":"6-7","wt":243,"home":"Broo